---
description: Block deletion when a record id is referenced by another collection
alwaysApply: true
---

# Referential delete restriction

Do not delete a record when its id is stored on another collection. This applies to base data (lookups) and every related table, until the user explicitly lifts the rule.

- Before any delete, check every foreign key that points at the record, including nested paths such as `verificationLogs.changedBy`.
- If any reference exists, throw `ApiError.conflict` (409) and name the collections that use it.
- Do not cascade-delete dependents, and do not clear the foreign key, in order to force the delete.
- A record with no remaining references may be deleted.
- Use `assertNotReferenced` from `src/common/utils/reference-guard.ts`. When adding a relation, add it to the delete guard of the referenced model.
